UPDATE lessons SET title='Year 4, Week 36, Lesson 1: Choosing a theme for our showcase', data=json_patch(data,'{"child_mission":"Choosing a creative showcase theme unifies artworks and performances across forms. Criteria might include clarity for audience, feasibility in the space and inclusion of visual, music, drama and dance items. Themes should be school-safe and achievable.","coming_soon":null,"duration_minutes":55,"evidence_instructions":"Save the independent response, specific revisions and both short-answer explanations; record oral evidence for speaking tasks.","explicit_teaching":null,"extension":"Apply the same arts idea to a new artwork or performance, then compare two choices for clarity of effect.","follow_up_challenges":null,"guided_practice":"PRACTISE BEFORE READING THE FEEDBACK\nPropose a theme with one item idea for each of two art forms and one feasibility check.\n\nFEEDBACK\nStrong answer: Theme named; two form ideas linked; check such as ''fits 30-minute runtime.''\n\nWATCH FOR\nPicking a huge theme no one can stage. Feasibility matters.","hoard_words":null,"independent_task":"INDEPENDENT EVIDENCE\nFacilitate a family/class vote on two theme options using written criteria; record the winner and why.\n\nWrite a short reflection naming one artistic choice you changed and why. Movement or instrument work is optional, adult-supervised and can be described instead.","interactive_activities":null,"learning_area":"Creative Arts","learning_intention":"Choosing a creative showcase theme unifies artworks and performances across forms. Criteria might include clarity for audience, feasibility in the space and inclusion of visual, music, drama and dance items. Themes should be school-safe and achievable.","lesson_number":1,"lesson_role":"Explore and learn","materials":["Paper or typed answer space","Pencil","Optional: scrap paper, crayons, safe classroom instruments or clear movement space with an adult nearby"],"offline_alternative":"Use paper and pencil to complete the original task, then retain a photograph or short parent observation as evidence.","outcome_codes":["CA2-VIS-01"],"parent_notes":"Parent: Marking guidance for the independent task: Facilitate a family/class vote on two theme options using written criteria; record the winner and why. Accept equivalent original responses that show the same skill.\n\nParent: Written model 1: Original response on new material: Strong answer: Theme named; two form ideas linked; check such as ''fits 30-minute runtime.'' Reasoning: I used showcase theme by attending to selection criteria rather than copying the worked model.\n\nParent: Written model 2: Common error: Picking a huge theme no one can stage. Feasibility matters. Correction: Strong answer: Theme named; two form ideas linked; check such as ''fits 30-minute runtime.'' Why: the correction restores accurate use of showcase theme.\n\nParent: Likely misconception: Picking a huge theme no one can stage. Feasibility matters. Keep sample answers out of the child role.\n\nParent: Short-answer focus 1: Produce a fresh example demonstrating showcase theme on new material (not the worked model). Explain the particular words, sources or choices that make it work.\n\nParent: Short-answer focus 2: Name one likely error with showcase theme, correct it, and explain why the correction helps a reader or audience.\n\nParent: Marking notes: Require independently produced work with a specific supporting detail. / Require misconception + correction + purpose-linked reason..","pass":1,"pass_mark":0.9,"planner_fields":null,"planner_intro":null,"planner_title":null,"printable_resource":null,"quiz":[{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Strong answer: Theme named; two form ideas linked; check such as ''fits 30-minute runtime.'' This matches the lesson skill for showcase theme.","options":["Strong answer: Theme named; two form ideas linked; check such as ''fits 30-minute runtime.''","Picking a huge theme no one can stage. Feasibility matters.","Say it looks nice with no element or technique named.","Copy the example artwork or script and call that independent work."],"question":"Propose a theme with one item idea for each of two art forms and one feasibility check. Which response is most accurate?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":1,"explanation":"Picking a huge theme no one can stage. Feasibility matters. That misconception weakens accuracy; the other choices align with the lesson idea.","options":["Careful use of selection criteria with clear evidence.","Picking a huge theme no one can stage. Feasibility matters.","Choosing a creative showcase theme unifies artworks and performances across forms. Criteria might include clarity for audience, feasibility in the space and…","Strong answer: Theme named; two form ideas linked; check such as ''fits 30-minute runtime.''"],"question":"Which statement is a common mistake when practising showcase theme?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":3,"explanation":"Understanding is shown by new evidence and named selection criteria, not by copying the model.","options":["Repeat the worked example wording with no new evidence.","Choose randomly because any option could be right.","Invent a sacred First Nations design without permission or guidance.","Apply the idea with new evidence and name the selection criteria used."],"question":"A learner is practising showcase theme. Which approach best shows understanding?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":3,"explanation":"Strong answer: Theme named; two form ideas linked; check such as ''fits 30-minute runtime.'' uses elements, techniques and audience effect appropriately for this lesson.","options":["Picking a huge theme no one can stage. Feasibility matters.","Say it looks nice with no element or technique named.","Copy the example artwork or script and call that independent work.","Strong answer: Theme named; two form ideas linked; check such as ''fits 30-minute runtime.''"],"question":"Which response best shows careful thinking about showcase theme?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":1,"explanation":"Strong answers name specific evidence and what it shows.","options":["Picking a huge theme no one can stage. Feasibility matters.","Name a specific source, cue or example and say what it shows about showcase theme.","Make a bigger claim without naming any source or cue.","Copy a classmate’s sentence with no local detail."],"question":"Which habit strengthens evidence about selection criteria?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":2,"explanation":"The stronger choice matches the taught idea with concrete detail.","options":["Invent a sacred First Nations design without permission or guidance.","Say it looks nice with no element or technique named.","Example: Theme ''Connections'' allows a friendship painting, a round about teamwork, a short conflict-resolution scene and a motif dance…","Picking a huge theme no one can stage. Feasibility matters."],"question":"Using this lesson idea — Choosing a creative showcase theme unifies artworks and performances across forms. Criteria might include… — which choice is best?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":1,"explanation":"Respect and accuracy mean checking evidence and honouring limits/protocols.","options":["Treat every online claim as equally reliable.","Check facts/cues, acknowledge limits, and avoid inventing details.","Invent missing details to make the answer sound complete.","Ignore safety or cultural protocols to finish faster."],"question":"Which action shows respect and accuracy together?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Independence requires a new example that still uses the skill.","options":["Facilitate a family/class vote on two theme options using written criteria; record the winner and why.","Retype the worked example with no new example.","Copy the example artwork or script and call that independent work.","Picking a huge theme no one can stage. Feasibility matters."],"question":"Which task best shows independent use of showcase theme?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"explanation":"Independent evidence on new material demonstrates the skill; copying the model does not.","marking_guide":"Require independently produced work with a specific supporting detail.","question":"Produce a fresh example demonstrating showcase theme on new material (not the worked model). Explain the particular words, sources or choices that make it work.","sample_answer":"Original response on new material: Strong answer: Theme named; two form ideas linked; check such as ''fits 30-minute runtime.'' Reasoning: I used showcase theme by attending to selection criteria rather than copying the worked model.","type":"short_answer"},{"explanation":"A useful correction changes the inaccurate idea or method and explains why.","marking_guide":"Require misconception + correction + purpose-linked reason.","question":"Name one likely error with showcase theme, correct it, and explain why the correction helps a reader or audience.","sample_answer":"Common error: Picking a huge theme no one can stage. Feasibility matters. Correction: Strong answer: Theme named; two form ideas linked; check such as ''fits 30-minute runtime.'' Why: the correction restores accurate use of showcase theme.","type":"short_answer"}],"resources":null,"response_prompt":"Include your independent artwork or performance notes and reflection, with reasons where requested.","review_status":"unreviewed","seed_key":"s2-arts-y4-w36-l1","sort_activity":null,"source_note":"Proposed Stage 2 NESA Creative Arts alignment using catalogue outcome codes (CA2-*); content-point mapping remains pending. First Nations arts content requires local Aboriginal educator or Custodian guidance before acceptance; do not invent sacred designs.","spelling":null,"spelling_focus":null,"stage":"S2","stage_hints":{"accept":["Today you will practise showcase theme.","Read the mission before you start making or performing.","Keep the audience effect of your choice in view."],"guided":["Attempt the guided prompt without looking ahead.","Afterwards, compare your reasons with the feedback.","Adjust anything that does not name an effect clearly."],"learn":["Study how the first demonstration is built.","Point to the element or technique that carries the idea.","Then write the reason without copying every sentence."],"quiz":["Read every option before you choose.","Eliminate answers that ignore elements, safety or respectful practice.","Prefer a named artistic reason over a guess that merely looks colourful."],"submit":["Confirm that your choice and reason are both present.","Proofread element names and safety notes.","Make sure the final evidence matches the lesson purpose."],"teach0":["Read the stage title and find the worked example.","Name one exact element, technique or cue before you decide.","Think through the small prompt before opening the comparison."],"teach1":["Return to the example and list the key artistic choices.","Say what each choice does for the artwork or audience.","A final praise word alone is weaker than a named effect."],"teach2":["Compare a weak choice with a stronger one.","Change the element or technique, not only the decoration.","Name the mistake you are repairing."],"teach3":["Choose a fresh subject or piece that still uses the same skill.","Write one reason in your own words.","Do not retype the worked example as your answer."],"write":["Follow every part of the independent instructions.","Include original work notes and a short reflection.","Save work that shows the skill on new material."]},"subject":"Creative Arts Showcase","success_criteria":["I can use showcase theme with a specific example from this lesson.","I can identify selection criteria and explain why it matters.","I can practise multi-art independently on a new prompt.","I can notice audience needs and correct a likely mistake."],"suspense_builder":null,"teach_steps":[{"check":{"correct_index":1,"explanation":"Choosing a creative showcase theme unifies artworks and performances across forms. Criteria might include clarity for audience, feasibility in the space and inclusion of visual, music, drama and dance items. Themes should be school-safe and achievable. Supported responses name…","options":["A guess with no artistic reason.","Choosing a creative showcase theme unifies artworks and performances across forms. Criteria might include clarity for audience, feasibility in the space and inclusion of visual, music, drama and dance items. Themes should be school-safe and achievable.","A comment that only says it looks nice with no element named.","An answer copied without understanding."],"question":"Which choice best shows accurate use of this idea about showcase theme?","type":"multiple_choice"},"example":"WORKED MODEL\nExample: Theme ''Connections'' allows a friendship painting, a round about teamwork, a short conflict-resolution scene and a motif dance about joining pathways.\n\nTRY FIRST\nPropose a theme with one item idea for each of two art forms and one feasibility check.\n\nFEEDBACK\nStrong answer: Theme named; two form ideas linked; check such as ''fits 30-minute runtime.''","explain":"Choosing a creative showcase theme unifies artworks and performances across forms. Criteria might include clarity for audience, feasibility in the space and inclusion of visual, music, drama and dance items. Themes should be school-safe and achievable.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS\nThis helps the learner make intentional visual, music, drama or dance choices and name their effect, rather than saying an artwork is simply “nice”. Keep every claim linked to an element or technique.\n\nHOW TO WORK\nRead the worked example and name the elements, techniques or performance choices that carry the idea. Before looking at the correction, make your own attempt using the exact question provided. For movement or instruments, use a clear space, ask an adult to be nearby and stop if anything feels unsafe. You may always describe a choice instead of performing it. One deliberate artistic choice with a named effect is more useful than a longer praise sentence.","icon":"📖","notice":"Picking a huge theme no one can stage. Feasibility matters. Name the element or technique and its effect, not just decoration.","title":"Understand and demonstrate","visual":[{"alt":"Choosing a theme.","caption":"Vote with reasons.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#297a61\"/><g font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#263948\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\">Theme</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\">unifies forms</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"42\">Criteria</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"78\">clear feasible inclusive</text></g></svg>"}],"visual_before":[{"episode":{"scenes":[{"bg":"room","lines":[{"text":"I can see the example, but I am not sure which artistic choice matters most.","who":"pip"},{"text":"Name the element, technique or performance choice and the effect it creates before you decide.","who":"juno"},{"text":"I will try the prompt myself, then compare with the feedback.","who":"pip"},{"pause_after":true,"text":"Pause here. Use this example: Example: Theme ''Connections'' allows a friendship painting, a round about teamwork, a short conflict-resolution scene and Then write your own artistic reason.","who":"juno"}]}],"title":"Talk through the first model","transcript":"Pip: I can see the example, but I am not sure which artistic choice matters most.\nJuno: Name the element, technique or performance choice and the effect it creates before you decide.\nPip: I will try the prompt myself, then compare with the feedback.\nJuno: Pause here. Use this example: Example: Theme ''Connections'' allows a friendship painting, a round about teamwork, a short conflict-resolution scene and Then write your own artistic reason."}}]},{"check":{"correct_index":2,"explanation":"Make the arts idea visible: name the element, technique or performance choice you used and say what effect it creates. Supported responses name the element or technique and its effect.","options":["An answer copied without understanding.","A guess with no artistic reason.","Make the arts idea visible: name the element, technique or performance choice you used and say what effect it creates.","A comment that only says it looks nice with no element named."],"question":"Which choice best shows accurate use of this idea about showcase theme?","type":"multiple_choice"},"example":"WORKED MODEL\nExample: Theme ''Connections'' allows a friendship painting, a round about teamwork, a short conflict-resolution scene and a motif dance about joining pathways. Look at each line, sound, movement or role choice that carries the idea.\n\nTRY FIRST\nList the key artistic choices from the example and say what each one does for the audience or artwork.\n\nFEEDBACK\nThe most useful response names the element or technique and its effect, not only “it looks nice”.","explain":"Make the arts idea visible: name the element, technique or performance choice you used and say what effect it creates.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS\nThis helps the learner make intentional visual, music, drama or dance choices and name their effect, rather than saying an artwork is simply “nice”. Keep every claim linked to an element or technique.\n\nHOW TO WORK\nRead the worked example and name the elements, techniques or performance choices that carry the idea. Before looking at the correction, make your own attempt using the exact question provided. For movement or instruments, use a clear space, ask an adult to be nearby and stop if anything feels unsafe. You may always describe a choice instead of performing it. One deliberate artistic choice with a named effect is more useful than a longer praise sentence.","icon":"📖","notice":"Writing only a final praise 